rrent hand has potential to form concealed melds: I have a pair of W2, pair of B3, and other singles. I could try to build toward a concealed hand (Concealed Hand or Fully Concealed Hand) for extra points. My exposed meld already prevents Fully Concealed, but Concealed Hand (winning tile from others) is still possible. Passing keeps options open and avoids exposing another meld, which might restrict patterns (e.g., All Chows requires four chows, but I already have one exposed chow, so I could still get All Chows if I form three more chows, but exposing another chow reduces flexibility).  \n\nConsidering scoring patterns: My hand currently has no terminals or honors except the W2 in the exposed chow, but W2 is simple. So All Simples (2 points) is possible. Also, I have two pairs, could aim for Seven Pairs (24 points) but that's harder with exposed meld (Seven Pairs requires no melds, only pairs). With an exposed meld, Seven Pairs is impossible. So I am committed to a standard hand (4 melds + pair).  \n\nGiven the tile counts: Unshown tiles show many mid-suit tiles available (e.g., T2 (3), T3 (2 left), T4 (3), T5 (3), T6 (1), etc.). Bamboos also available. Winds and dragons are somewhat depleted (F1: 2 left, F3: 3 left, J1: 3 left). My hand has no honors currently.  \n\nReason: I should probably Pass. Chi T5 would expose another meld, locking me into a specific suit (Bamboo) for that chow, and it uses my only T4 and one T3. My hand after Chi would be fragmented: two pairs (W2 and B3) and three singles (W6, W7, T3). That's not a strong waiting shape. Passing allows me to draw a tile that might improve my hand\u2014maybe draw a W tile to work toward a Half Flush (W suit + honors, but I have no honors yet) or draw a B3 to make a pung, etc. Also, by not exposing another meld, I retain more flexibility for patterns like Mixed Straight, All Chows, etc. Since the prevailing wind is East and my seat wind is North, I have no wind pungs yet, so no extra points from those. My goal is to build a hand worth at least 8 points. With one exposed chow already, I need to plan patterns: All Simples (2) + maybe Self-Drawn (1) + Closed Wait (1) + Pure Double Chow (1) etc. might not reach 8. I need stronger patterns. Passing to draw gives a chance to improve.  \n\nAnswer: Pass"}
