ding W7 leaves W6, which might pair if I draw another W6 (1 left). Also, W7 is higher number, might be safer discard.  \nAlternatively, discard B2 is also fine. But B2 might have slight chance to form chow with B1/B3? B1 is 0 left, B3 I have two, so B2 could be used with B3 and B4? B4 is 0 left. So B2 is also dead.  \nGiven the game stage (many tiles have been played), I'll discard W7 to reduce W suit clutter while keeping pairs and sequence potential in T suit.\n\nAnswer: Play W7"}
